# beehiiv-react — Cursor Rules

Read SKILL.md in the repo root before making any changes. It is the canonical source of truth.

## Critical constraints — enforce these on every edit

- `BeehiivClient` is server-only. Never import it in hooks, components, or client bundles.
- React and react-dom are peer dependencies. Never add them to `dependencies`.
- All hooks must use `useBeehiiv()` for `apiUrl`. Never hardcode URLs.
- All hooks must use a `fetchIdRef` ref to guard stale responses.
- No `any` types. No `@ts-ignore`. TypeScript strict mode is enforced.
- No default exports except React components.
- ESM-only packages (chalk, ora, open) must be dynamically imported inside functions.
- New types must be registered in `src/types/index.ts` AND `src/index.ts`.
- Every PR must pass: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build`.

## Adding features — order of operations

**New endpoint:** types → `src/types/index.ts` → endpoint class → `BeehiivClient` → `src/index.ts` → tests
**New hook:** `src/hooks/use<Name>.ts` → `src/hooks/index.ts` → `src/index.ts` → tests
**New component:** `src/components/<Name>.tsx` → `src/components/index.ts` → `src/index.ts` → tests

## Test baseline: 126 passing tests across 14 files. Do not reduce this count.
